{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u,\\,z=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0,\\,1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,2,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2u+v,\\,y={u}^{2},\\,z={v}^{2}\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\,{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨2,\\,2(1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,1,\\,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={v}^{2},\\,y=2v,\\,z=4u\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{v}^{2},\\,2v,\\,4u⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨2(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,4,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-8,\\,0,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,2,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,4,\\,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=1+{e}^{u},\\,y=2-{e}^{v},\\,z=1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v}\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨1+{e}^{u},\\,2-{e}^{v},\\,1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+{e}^{u}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{u},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{u}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+{e}^{u}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-{e}^{u}-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,-{e}^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨{e}^{1},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨e,\\,0,\\,-e⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨0,\\,-{e}^{-1},\\,-{e}^{-1}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ e & 0 & -e \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-1} & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -e \\\\ -{e}^{-1} & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}e & -e \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}e & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,e,\\,-e⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,2e⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,2e,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-{e}^{2},\\,{e}^{-1},\\,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y={u}^{2}v,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,{u}^{2}v,\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2uv,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{u}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(1)(2),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,(1)^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-105544" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105544" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,\\,-4,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-3⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105544" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨1+v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}⟩$ at the point $(2,1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $(2,1,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1+v=2 \\\\ uv=1 \\\\ {u}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,v,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,u,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(2,1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,0,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨1+u,\\,2v,\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}⟩$ at the point $(2,-4,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $(2,-4,-3)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1+u=2 \\\\ 2v=-4 \\\\ {u}^{2}-{v}^{2}=-3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,-2) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-2) & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(2,-4,-3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,-2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2,\\,-2,\\,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,4,\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-v⟩$ at the point $(1,1,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $(1,1,2)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ {v}^{2}=1 \\\\ {u}^{2}-v=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) & =⟨0,\\,2(-1),\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,1,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-110060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,4,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-4,\\,1,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,2,\\,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u,\\,(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\n at the point $(1,1,\\sqrt{3}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $(2,3,4)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=1 \\\\ u=1 \\\\ (1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,1,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}((1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0,\\,-(1+{u}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =⟨2(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}),\\,1,\\,2(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =⟨(1+(1)^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}),\\,0,\\,-(1+(1)^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,1,\\sqrt{3})$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,4,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-110070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,4,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,2,\\,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,-2,\\,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,2,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,4,\\,-\\sqrt{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,v⟩$ at the point $(1,2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $(1,2,0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u+v=1 \\\\ 2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}=2 \\\\ v=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨1,\\,4(1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨1,\\,2(0),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,2,0)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,0)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-110546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2,\\,-1,\\,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-4⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,-4,\\,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,2,\\,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-110546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-4⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,u+v,\\,uv⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,1,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨2(1),\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨-2(1),\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=1$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n({1}^{2}-{1}^{2},\\,1+1,\\,1\\cdot 1)=(0,2,1),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,-4,\\,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot x+(-4)\\cdot (y-2)+4\\cdot (z-1) & =0 \\\\ -4y+4z+4 & =0 \\\\ -y+z+1 & =0 \\\\ y-z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4y+2z=1"] ["math" "x+y+z=1"] ["math" "x-y+4z=2"] ["math" "y+2z=-4"] ["math" "y-z=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y-z=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2{u}^{3},\\,u{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2uv,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨6(1)^{2},\\,{3}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,9,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨0,\\,2(1)(3),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,3)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,-12,\\,36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=3$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(1)^{3},\\,1(3)^{2},\\,2(3))=(2,9,6),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨18,\\,-12,\\,36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-9,\\,z-6⟩ & =0 \\\\ 18\\cdot (x-2)-12\\cdot (y-9)+36\\cdot (z-6) & =0 \\\\ 18x-12y+36z-144 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+6z-24 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+6z & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x-3y+z=144"] ["math" "3x-2y+6z=24"] ["math" "3x-y+3z=24"] ["math" "x-2y+3z=12"] ["math" "x-2y+z=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x-2y+6z=24"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2)=(0,2,2),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-2,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot x+(-2)\\cdot (y-2)+2\\cdot (z-2) & =0 \\\\ -2y+2z & =0 \\\\ y-z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109768" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109768" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2y+z=-2"] ["math" "x+y-z=0"] ["math" "y+z=2"] ["math" "y-2z=1"] ["math" "y-z=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109768" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y-z=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,{u}^{3}-uv⟩$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}-uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3{u}^{2}-v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}-uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,6) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3(2)^{2}-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,6⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,6) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,6)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,6) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=6$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2,\\,6,\\,{2}^{3}-(2)(6))=(2,6,-4),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-6,\\,2,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-6,\\,z+4⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-6)\\cdot (x-2)+2\\cdot (y-6)+1\\cdot (z+4) & =0 \\\\ -6x+2y+z+4 & =0 \\\\ 6x-2y-z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x-2y+z=2"] ["math" "6x-2y-z=4"] ["math" "6x-y-2z=2"] ["math" "x-3y+2z=4"] ["math" "x-y-z=3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6x-2y-z=4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4{u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,8u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4{u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,8(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,8⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨0,\\,(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi )\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,0,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=\\pi $ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(1),\\,(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,4(1)^{2})=(2,0,4),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨8,\\,0,\\,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 8\\cdot (x-2)+0\\cdot y+(-2)\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ 8x-2z-8 & =0 \\\\ 4x-z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-105594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x-z=0"] ["math" "4x-z=4"] ["math" "8x+y-2z=3"] ["math" "8x-y-2z=8"] ["math" "x-4z=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-105594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x-z=4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,z=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nat the point $(1,0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(1,0,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=0 \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨2(1),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) & =⟨0,\\,2(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,0)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,0) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,0,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,0,\\,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-1)+0\\cdot y+4\\cdot (z-1) & =0 \\\\ -2x+4z-2 & =0 \\\\ -x+2z-1 & =0 \\\\ x-2z & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x+2z=-2"] ["math" "x+y=-2"] ["math" "x+z=1"] ["math" "x-2y=1"] ["math" "x-2z=-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2z=-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nat the point $(-2,0,\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(-2,0,\\pi )$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-2 \\\\ u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=0 \\\\ v=\\pi \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=2 \\\\ v=\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=2$ and $v=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\pi ) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,\\pi )\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,\\pi ) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y,\\,z-\\pi ⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot (x+2)+1\\cdot y+2\\cdot (z-\\pi ) & =0 \\\\ y+2z-2\\pi  & =0 \\\\ y+2z & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+z=\\pi "] ["math" "2y-z=2\\pi "] ["math" "x+z=\\pi "] ["math" "y+2z=2\\pi "] ["math" "y-z=-\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+2z=2\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=uv,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,v\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nat the point $(1,4,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,uv⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(1,4,2)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=1 \\\\ {v}^{2}=4 \\\\ uv=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨2(1),\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨0,\\,2(2),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,4,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,-2,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-8,\\,-2,\\,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-4,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-8)\\cdot (x-1)+(-2)\\cdot (y-4)+8\\cdot (z-2) & =0 \\\\ -8x-2y+8z & =0 \\\\ 4x+y-4z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+2y-3z=0"] ["math" "2x-y+z=2"] ["math" "4x+y-4z=0"] ["math" "x+y-z=-2"] ["math" "x-y+z=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109829" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x+y-4z=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nat the point $(4,1,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(4,1,4)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=4 \\\\ {v}^{2}=1 \\\\ u+2v=4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=2 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=2$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨2(2),\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨0,\\,2(1),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-1,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-4)+(-8)\\cdot (y-1)+8\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ -2x-8y+8z-16 & =0 \\\\ -x-4y+4z-8 & =0 \\\\ x+4y-4z & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+y-2z=-4"] ["math" "2x+y=4"] ["math" "x+2y=8"] ["math" "x+4y-4z=-8"] ["math" "x-4y+2z=8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+4y-4z=-8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,y={u}^{2},\\,z=2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nat the point $(0,1,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩,\\,u\\ge 0,\\,0\\le v<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(0,1,-2)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=0 \\\\ {u}^{2}=1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=-2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0,\\,-2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,2(1),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨1\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,0,\\,-2(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi )\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-1,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot x+2\\cdot (y-1)+2\\cdot (z+2) & =0 \\\\ 2y+2z+2 & =0 \\\\ y+z & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10efd9bc07d8726d5824cd077bc259054ee80f0fe9cc3861305c107f68a8e55b"} {"question" "q-109831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2y-2z=1"] ["math" "x+z=2"] ["math" "x-2z=1"] ["math" "y+z=-1"] ["math" "y-2z=2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "q-109831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+z=-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/state.json" "file_sha256" "c633ee94a60f588dfa47c1715531de9e02ab9a159befe4b328cee9d4e535d4c3"} {"question" "e-8938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u, \\quad \ny=1+u^2, \\quad\nz=v^2\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/example-8938.json" "file_sha256" "c4ee8e1033a872a41da57755da5f52ec364b626f7ce4660346015b28a68cc781"} {"question" "e-8938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: 1 + u^2, \\: v^2\\big\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,-4,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/example-8938.json" "file_sha256" "c4ee8e1033a872a41da57755da5f52ec364b626f7ce4660346015b28a68cc781"} {"question" "e-8939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/e81d44c7891de67ac97b59abe1bd1c2b67335bb809e3dc5031a6c